        "content": "# Ideation & Product Rationale — SKI-19: Upgrade McpFn and clean up obsolete MCP Worker compatibility configuration\n\n**Issue:** [SKI-19](https://linear.app/21n/issue/SKI-19/upgrade-mcpfn-and-clean-up-obsolete-mcp-worker-compatibility)\n\n## Context and motivating problem\n\nSkillplane's full development topology deployment stopped when Cloudflare validated the regional MCP Worker. The Worker bundle executed a mixed Zod dependency graph introduced through the current McpFn and MCP SDK package path and failed with `TypeError: Class2 is not a constructor`.\n\nThe durable package correction is tracked in [MCP-4](https://linear.app/21n/issue/MCP-4/make-mcpfn-cloudflare-worker-bundles-resilient-to-mixed-zod-entry). Skillplane still owns adopting the corrected published packages, removing obsolete Cloudflare compatibility configuration, and proving that the complete consumer deployment succeeds.\n\nThe current MCP configuration also carries `allow_eval_during_startup` with compatibility date `2026-05-03`. Local workerd rejects this redundant flag because the behavior is already default after 2025-06-01. This is separate from the Zod initialization failure but belongs in the same consumer cleanup and validation pass.\n\n## Target users and stakeholders\n\n* Skillplane maintainers operating the development topology.\n* Developers using the regional MCP Worker and local runtime.\n* McpFn maintainers handing off the corrected package release.\n* Operators validating Cloudflare deployments and authentication behavior.\n* MCP clients that depend on the endpoint retaining its existing authentication requirements.\n\n## Use cases and user journeys\n\n### Skillplane dependency adoption\n\n1. Receive the corrected McpFn package versions from MCP-4.\n2. Review the package and lockfile diff.\n3. Upgrade the coordinated McpFn packages.\n4. Remove temporary consumer workarounds, if any exist.\n5. Run focused MCP and topology validation.\n\n### Configuration cleanup