uire authentication.\n* Evidence clearly identifies which local, cloud-development, and production layers were verified.\n\n## Decisions and rationale\n\n* **Decision:** Block implementation on the published MCP-4 release.\n  * **Rationale:** The durable runtime correction belongs upstream and should not be duplicated in Skillplane.\n* **Decision:** Pair dependency adoption with compatibility-configuration cleanup.\n  * **Rationale:** Both affect MCP Worker startup and can be validated in one bounded consumer rollout.\n* **Decision:** Require real Worker execution and controlled development deployment.\n  * **Rationale:** Dry-run bundling did not reproduce the startup failure.\n\n## Product, UX, and operational considerations\n\nNo user-facing workflow should change. Operators should gain a reliable, complete topology deployment path. Authentication behavior is a preservation requirement, not a redesign opportunity.\n\n## Assumptions\n\n* MCP-4 will publish coordinated package versions usable by Skillplane.\n* The obsolete compatibility flag is not needed for another supported compatibility date.\n* No permanent alias has landed on the current branch; other incident-response branches or environments may still require inspection.\n\n## Open questions\n\n* Which package versions will MCP-4 publish?\n* Should a full development topology deployment become a recurring release gate?\n* Are any external environment-specific configs generated outside the repository's current topology renderer?\n\n## Goals\n\n* Adopt the corrected McpFn release.\n* Remove obsolete and temporary MCP Worker compatibility configuration.\n* Restore complete development topology deployment.\n* Preserve MCP authentication behavior.\n\n## Non-goals\n\n* Implement the upstream McpFn or MCP SDK fix.\n* Change tool contracts or tenant policy.\n* General dependency upgrades.\n* Production deployment during backlog capture.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n* Coordinated McpFn packages and lockfile are upgraded.\n* No consumer-local Zod alias or shim remains.\n* The obsolete compatibility flag is absent from source and generated configs.\n* Workerd reaches ready state.\n* The full controlled development topology deploys, including MCP.\n* Smoke validation confirms authentication is still required.\n* Validation reporting distinguishes unverified production status.",
