      "b": {
        "content": "# Architecture & Delivery Plan — SKI-19: Upgrade McpFn and clean up obsolete MCP Worker compatibility configuration\n\n**Issue:** [SKI-19](https://linear.app/21n/issue/SKI-19/upgrade-mcpfn-and-clean-up-obsolete-mcp-worker-compatibility)\n\n## Current-state constraints\n\nSkillplane currently consumes McpFn `0.0.4` packages and directly uses Zod in its MCP application and shared schemas. The current MCP SDK path introduced through McpFn evaluates runtime schemas from `zod/v4`, producing a broken initialization order in the Wrangler bundle. The application also includes a now-redundant Cloudflare compatibility flag.\n\nThe deployment pipeline renders regional Wrangler configurations and then deploys the topology. Editing generated files alone would be overwritten and would not correct the source of truth.\n\n## Proposed architecture and ownership\n\n```text\nMCP-4 publishes corrected McpFn packages\n  ↓\nSkillplane updates coordinated dependencies and lockfile\n  ↓\nSkillplane removes obsolete source configuration\n  ↓\nTopology renderer regenerates regional configs\n  ↓\nFocused tests → workerd startup → full dev topology deploy → auth smoke\n```\n\n### Component responsibilities\n\n* **McpFn:** corrected protocol/runtime package boundary and Worker startup regression coverage.\n* **Skillplane MCP package:** consume published McpFn APIs without aliases or internal dependency knowledge.\n* **Wrangler source configuration:** define only currently supported compatibility behavior.\n* **Topology renderer:** propagate source configuration consistently to regional generated files.\n* **Deployment orchestration:** include the MCP Worker in the full topology path.\n* **Smoke checks:** verify endpoint reachability and authentication preservation.\n\n## Dependency and interface changes\n\n* Upgrade `@mcpfn/core`, `@mcpfn/auth`, and `@mcpfn/testing` together when MCP-4 specifies the release set.\n* Review any direct `@modelcontextprotocol/sdk` compatibility requirements.\n* Do not add an absolute alias into `node_modules`.\n* Remove any temporary local Zod normalization once the package upgrade proves unnecessary.\n* Preserve the MCP Worker request, transport, and authorization contracts.\n\n## Configuration data flow\n\n```text\nmcp/wrangler.jsonc and deployment templates\n  └─ render-development-topology-config\n       └─ regional generated Wrangler JSON\n            └─ development-topology-deployment\n                 └─ Wrangler/workerd and Cloudflare upload\n```\n\nThe obsolete flag must be removed at the source and verified absent at each generated output boundary.\n\n## Security and authorization\n\n* Do not alter authorization scopes, token validation, or tenant routing.\n* Use non-production bindings for local startup validation.\n* After deployment, confirm unauthenticated MCP access remains rejected.\n* Do not print secrets or deployment credentials in logs or issue updates.\n\n## Reliability and observability\n\nValidation should record independent checkpoints:\n\n1. configuration render succeeds;\n2. dependency and lockfile state is reproducible;\n3. focused unit/type/package checks pass;\n4. Worker bundle is produced;\n5. workerd reaches ready state;\n6. Cloudflare development upload and startup succeed;\n7. authentication smoke passes.\n\nA failure at one checkpoint must not be reported as evidence for later checkpoints.\n\n## Migration plan\n\n 1. Wait for MCP-4 to publish corrected package versions and notes.\n 2. Inspect the package diff and compatibility constraints.\n 3. Upgrade the coordinated McpFn dependencies and refresh the frozen lockfile.\n 4. Remove `allow_eval_during_startup` from source configuration and renderer inputs.\n 5. Regenerate topology outputs.\n 6. Search for stale aliases, flags, and generated copies.\n 7. Run focused MCP tests and static checks.\n 8. Start the rendered Worker under workerd.\n 9. Perform a controlled full development topology deployment.\n10. Run authentication