  "comments": [
    {
      "id": "5cb26140-0028-4b82-aaef-8a5a7eb645fa",
      "body": "Fixed in PR: https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/204\n\n`@mcpfn/core` and `@mcpfn/auth` now inline the MCP SDK and a single pinned Zod runtime into their published bundles, so a Cloudflare Worker can bundle McpFn next to a root `zod` without any consumer-side `zod`/`zod/v4` alias or shim, eliminating the `Class2 is not a constructor` startup crash. Schema validation additionally falls back from Ajv to `@cfworker/json-schema` on runtimes that forbid runtime code generation (workerd), so tool-serving Workers boot and serve calls. A representative workerd startup + `tools/call` regression test (`cloudflare:worker-startup`) is wired into `npm run gate:mcpfn-release`, which passes end to end. `@mcpfn/client` stays Node-targeted because its stdio transport depends on `child_process`.\n",
      "bodyTruncated": false,
